"""📐 Screen-part rules: what each part of a premium WORK app must hold and how it is laid out (the user, 2026-11-14:
the landing sections got their rule sets (sections.py); "do it for admin, CRM, ERP, POS, CMS, dashboards too").

COMMON: the rules every app screen keeps. RULES[part]: job (what it is for), content (what it must hold), rules
(shape, alignment, density, states), never, phone (how it changes on a phone). Parts are pagebuild / widgets parts.
Drawn from the user's reference folders (D:/SAGE_CDSRA_POC, 2026-11-14) and design-system guidance (Material, Carbon,
Atlassian: tables, empty states, forms). The 4B gets brief(part) for each part it plans."""

COMMON = [
    "One job per screen: the main tool is the biggest part, top left after the greeting / title; supporting parts after it.",
    "A real head: the screen's title, one status line (today's date, how many need action), the main action button at the right.",
    "Numbers right-aligned in tables, with units and the same decimals; money with its currency; dates one format.",
    "Every status is a coloured pill with a word (never colour alone): green done / paid, amber pending, red overdue / failed, grey draft.",
    "Density: tables 44-52 px rows, cards 16-24 px padding, 12-16 px gaps; labels 12-13 px muted, values 20-32 px bold.",
    "Every list and table has a search or filter when it has more than 8 rows, and a row action (view, edit, more).",
    "States: an empty part says what will appear and the action to add the first one; never a blank box.",
    "Charts: one message each, a title that says it, the period switch at its top right, the latest value called out.",
    "Colour: the brand accent for the main action and the main series; status colours only for status; a calm surface.",
    "Phone: the side menu becomes a bottom tab bar of 4-5; tables become cards; the main tool still comes first.",
]

